From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kamil Monicz <kamil@monicz.dev>
Date: Sat, 07 Nov 2026 06:08:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Bound pyclass freelists and restore GC tracking

Keep destroyed allocations in bounded static storage and transfer them
through a sealed ownership interface. Use the GIL for CPython cache access;
free-threaded-compatible builds retain the native allocator hooks instead
of contending on a class-wide cache.

Honor the complete declared capacity and restore GC tracking only after
the concrete Rust subtype and its bases have been initialized. Preserve
the ordinary constructor path for classes without an active cache.
---
